1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
You say yes to everything.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,320
Staying late, lending money,

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,300
going to the thing
you did not want to go to.

4
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,750
Yes, yes, yes.

5
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:11,630
Even when your whole body is saying no.

6
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:13,740
So here is the question.

7
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:18,880
What happens if, for seven days,
you say no to everyone?

8
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:22,740
Not rude, not angry, just no.

9
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,210
Let’s see.

10
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:27,820
Monday, 5:30. Your boss walks over.

11
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,940
“Can you stay a bit late tonight?”

12
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:33,570
Normally you say, “Of course,”
before he finishes the sentence.

13
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:36,820
Today you say, “No.”

14
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:38,150
He blinks.

15
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:40,130
Then he says, “Okay.”

16
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:42,240
That’s it. “Okay.”

17
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:45,710
You prepared for war and got a shrug.

18
00:00:45,710 --> 00:00:47,870
Tuesday. Your friend calls.

19
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:49,940
“Can you help me move on Saturday?”

20
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:51,140
“No.”

21
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:52,340
And you hear it.

22
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:54,100
That small pause.

23
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:57,290
The one that says,
“I thought we were close.”

24
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:58,990
Now your stomach drops.

25
00:00:58,990 --> 00:01:03,030
Nobody did anything to you
and you still feel guilty.

26
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:04,320
Remember that feeling.

27
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:06,390
It comes back later.

28
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:08,420
Wednesday, your mom calls.

29
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:10,330
“Are you coming for Sunday lunch?”

30
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:11,530
“No.”

31
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:13,100
She does not argue.

32
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,680
She says, “Fine.”

33
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:16,580
In a voice that is not fine.

34
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:19,040
Then she calls again. And again.

35
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:22,320
By evening, you have nine missed calls
and one text.

36
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:23,960
“Are you alive?”

37
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:26,870
Day three. The world has not ended.

38
00:01:26,870 --> 00:01:28,880
But your phone is exhausted.

39
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,280
Thursday, a coworker pops by.

40
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:33,680
“Lunch? That new place just opened.”

41
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:34,940
“No.”

42
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:37,790
And the second it leaves your mouth,
you know.

43
00:01:37,790 --> 00:01:39,110
You wanted to go.

44
00:01:39,110 --> 00:01:42,240
You have been wanting to try
that place for weeks.

45
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,070
Here is the problem
with saying no to everything.

46
00:01:45,070 --> 00:01:47,920
You also say no
to the things you actually want.

47
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:52,570
Friday. A tourist asks,
“Sorry, could you take our photo?”

48
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:53,860
“No.”

49
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:55,060
They look hurt.

50
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:56,260
And you feel terrible.

51
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:57,860
So you run after them.

52
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:59,120
You take the photo,

53
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,900
and it is the happiest
you have been all week.

54
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:05,070
Why?
Because this time, you chose it.

55
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:07,630
Same yes, different reason.

56
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:10,840
Not fear, choice.

57
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:14,100
Saturday, your boss texts,
“Need that report tonight.”

58
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:15,520
You do not say no.

59
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:17,300
You do not panic yes, either.

60
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:21,250
You say, “I can’t tonight.
I can send it first thing tomorrow.”

61
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:23,250
He says, “Perfect.”

62
00:02:23,250 --> 00:02:24,880
That is the one that works.

63
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:28,170
Not a flat no. A real answer.

64
00:02:28,170 --> 00:02:31,040
Sunday. So what happened?

65
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:32,720
A few people were annoyed.

66
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:34,470
One went quiet for a day.

67
00:02:34,470 --> 00:02:37,620
And one or two actually
respected you more.

68
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:39,310
Nobody’s life ended.

69
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:40,770
Here’s what I noticed.

70
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:43,140
Most of our yeses are not kindness.

71
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:44,660
They are fear.

72
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:47,340
Fear that people will stop liking us.

73
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,480
That guilty feeling on Tuesday.

74
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:53,270
It was not proof you did something wrong.

75
00:02:53,270 --> 00:02:56,080
It was just what changing
a habit feels like.

76
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:58,800
So, do not say no to everyone.

77
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,080
Try this instead.

78
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:03,860
For one week, when someone asks you
for something, say,

79
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:06,900
“Let me think and get back to you.”
That is all.

80
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:11,420
It gives you a pause,
and in that pause, you get to choose.

81
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:15,620
Yes, no, or “yes, but not like that.”

82
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:18,400
You decide on purpose.

83
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:22,010
So, what if you said no to everyone
for seven days?

84
00:03:22,010 --> 00:03:25,950
You would be tired, a little guilty,
and a lot more honest.

85
00:03:25,950 --> 00:03:28,820
Now tell me in the comments:
what is one thing you said yes to

86
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:31,750
this week that you really
wanted to say no to?

87
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:32,950
I’ll go first.

88
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:36,250
I said no to food because
I honestly do not want it.

89
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:37,880
See you in the next one.

